nder water is conditional, so base 30 with the note. Underwater Navigation is the catalog row Navigation: Underwater. The four Coalition Navy skills exist in the catalog. Swimming 75% +1% per level from Natural Abilities is stored as the Swimming skill at those figures (the greot-hunter precedent). || RELATED: one at levels 1, 4, 8, 12 and 15; Forced March is a Military row, so Military is granted with only Forced March to keep it reachable. All new skills start at first level. SECONDARY: one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. || PSIONICS: Major Psychic with Hydrokinesis, Empathy, Telepathy, Presence Sense, Levitation, Resist Hunger, Resist Thirst and Mind Block, granted by name; I.S.P. M.E. x4 plus 1D6 per level. || EQUIPMENT: 1D4 large sacks stored as large-sack. The two giant satchels and the 3-5 gallon water skin have no catalog row and are a restriction line. MONEY: printed only as understanding the concept of money; no figure, so starting_money 0. || NOT STORED: also known as Crab-Man and Devil Crab, size 5-6 feet tall and 10-15 feet in diameter, weight 700 to 1,200 pounds, life span (males 3D6+40, females 3D6+70), reproduction, group sizes, slave market value 2D4x10,000, habitat, allies and enemies are in GM Notes. Experience Level 1D4+3 for NPCs is a population figure."
