## Lore

Crab Warriors are semi-intelligent alien predators that live along beaches
and river banks. They only look like crabs: a hunched, humanoid upper body
with two outsized pincer arms, short horns over sunken eyes, six stubby legs
where a human''s two would be, and a sandy exoskeleton about as tough as
ceramic tank armor. They live on shore but swim superbly, spending half or
more of their lives underwater.

They range along the Gulf coast and the Caribbean, and in summer follow the
big rivers north as far as the Great Lakes, where many join pirate crews.
Pirates prize them as fighters and underwater raiders who cost far less than
power armor or a mini-sub.

A Crab Warrior hunts for meat and bones and finds humanoids the easiest prey
of all. Its favorite trick is the ambush: lurking in shallows or in a sealed
sand dome, then dragging a victim into the water to drown. Bands range from a
handful to a clan of a hundred or more. They have no use for technology or
magic, and speak in squeals, growls, clicks and whistles.

As characters they are childlike: simple, hungry, superstitious, quick to
anger when teased, and fond of wrestling, play-fighting and real fighting.
They are ruthless in battle but know when to retreat.

## GM Notes

Starting money: the entry prints no starting money, so none is stored.

Also known as Crab-Man and Devil Crab. Size 5-6 feet (1.5 to 1.8 m) tall and
10-15 feet (3 to 4.6 m) in diameter; weight 700 to 1,200 pounds (315 to 540
kg). Females are 10% larger than males and 33% less aggressive.

Life span: males 3D6+40 years, females 3D6+70. Full maturity at age 12.
Females lay 1D6 eggs each spring and sit on them for three months; both
parents raise the young until age six.

Groups: small attack groups 1D6+4, medium bands 3D4+8, large groups 4D4+12,
clans or tribes 2D4x10+20.

Slave market value 2D4x10,000 as fighters, pirate raiders, gladiators,
guardians of underwater lairs and heavy labor.

Habitat: sandy or gravel beaches and river banks in warm climates, migrating
to temperate regions in summer; the Gulf Coast and Caribbean islands, the
coast of Atlantis, and the seas and rivers of Africa and the Indian
subcontinent.

Allies: mostly their own kind, sometimes humans and D-Bees, especially other
aquatic beings and pirate crews. Enemies: most humanoids are prey; Dead Boys
and Free Quebec Glitter Boys are the enemy; they dislike Bayou Ursines,
Psi-Stalkers and most mammalian people, hate Deer Horn, Butter Trolls and
Dramins, and count Horune Pirates as hated rivals who enslave them.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'crab-warrior');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'crab-warrior';

